  "worked_solution": "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<-2.17)=P(Z\\le -2.17)=Φ(-2.17).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14254773/assets/eb01b718ca3f376cf50b7d3b7729b82dbc5b4a489519aedb06b15deacf466660.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(-2.17)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $-2.1$ and the column that corresponds to $0.07.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0116\\,$ | $\\,0.0113\\,$ | $\\,0.0110\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0150\\,$ | $\\,0.0146\\,$ | $\\,0.0143\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0192\\,$ | $\\,0.0188\\,$ | $\\,0.0183\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le -2.17)=Φ(-2.17)=0.0150.\n$$",
